abstract:
We present methods for computing the explicit decomposition of the minimal simple affine $W$-algebra $W_k(\mathfrak g, 	heta)$ at a conformal level $k$ as a module for its maximal affine subalgebra $\mathcal V_k(\mathfrak g^{
atural})$. A particular emphasis is given on the application of affine fusion rules to the determination of branching rules. In almost all cases when $\mathfrak g^{
atural}$ is a semisimple Lie algebra, we show that, for a suitable conformal level $k$, $W_k(\mathfrak g, 	heta)$ is isomorphic to an extension of $\mathcal V_k(\mathfrak g^{
atural})$ by its simple module. We are able to prove that in certain cases $W_k(\mathfrak g, 	heta)$ is a simple current extension of $\mathcal V_k(\mathfrak g^{
atural})$. In order to analyze more complicated non simple current extensions at conformal levels, we present an explicit realization of the simple $W$-algebra $W_{k}(sl(4), 	heta)$ at $k=-8/3$. We prove, as conjectured in arXiv:1407.1527, that $W_{k}(sl(4), 	heta)$ is isomorphic to the vertex algebra $\mathcal R^{(3)}$, and construct infinitely many singular vectors using screening operators. We also construct a new family of simple current modules for the vertex algebra $V_k (sl(n))$ at certain admissible levels and for $V_k (sl(m | n)), m
e n, m,n\geq 1$ at arbitrary levels.
